# Line endings, pinned so every machine and every checkout agrees.
#
# Installed by init-project.sh, and the scaffold ships it because a project created from here should not
# have to rediscover that a cross-platform tree needs this.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. With no .gitattributes, line endings depend on each machine's `core.autocrlf` setting,
# so the same commit can be checked out with different bytes on a Windows machine and on a Mac or Linux
# one. Three consequences:
#
#   - A content fingerprint, a canonical byte comparison or a digest computed over TEXT differs between
#     machines. Pin the endings BEFORE something hashes a file, not after the digests disagree.
#   - A diff shows every line of a file as changed when only its endings moved, which hides the real
#     change inside the noise - the failure mode where a reviewer stops reading.
#   - bash reads a CR as part of the line, so a script or config file with CRLF endings runs differently.
#
# `text=auto` normalises to LF in the repository and lets git decide the working tree. Every text file is
# therefore stored identically and compared identically, whatever a contributor's git config says.

* text=auto

# Explicit, because auto-detection gets these wrong and a wrong guess corrupts them.
*.json      text
*.md        text
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
# Read by bash, with no extension to match above: a CR turns `'-'` into a value that is not the sentinel.
gate.config text eol=lf
gate.config.pristine text eol=lf
pre-push    text eol=lf
# Every git hook, by folder, because hooks have no extension and bash runs them. In a clone made with
# core.autocrlf=true, tests/hooks/pre-commit came out with 61 CRLF endings while pre-push, named above, had
# none (research-claude-manager, 2026-11-10). The scaffold keeps its hooks in mechanisms/hooks/;
# init-project.sh installs them into a project's tests/hooks/.
mechanisms/hooks/* text eol=lf
tests/hooks/*      text eol=lf
# Read by cmd.exe, which needs CRLF: a .cmd or .bat with LF endings can skip or merge lines.
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf

# Binary: never converted, never diffed as text. `-text` is what stops a checkout from rewriting bytes.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.webp      binary
*.ico       binary
*.ttf       binary
*.otf       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.svg       text
*.pdf       binary
*.zip       binary
